# Ednov-mobile: Expo Router & Navigation

Use **expo-router** (file-based routing). Do not introduce raw React Navigation navigators for screen structure; use the file system and layouts.

## Route structure

- Routes live under `app/`. Use route groups with parentheses: `(tabs)`, `(auth)`, etc.
- Use `_layout.tsx` for layout and nesting; keep layout files thin (structure and providers only).
- Dynamic segments: use `[id].tsx` (or `[slug].tsx`); access params via `useLocalSearchParams()` from expo-router.

## Navigation

- Use `<Link href="...">` for declarative navigation, or `router.push()`, `router.replace()`, `router.back()` from `expo-router` for imperative navigation.
- Prefer `href` paths that match the file structure (e.g. `/(tabs)/two`, `/modal`).
- Deep linking: follow Expo Router and React Navigation deep linking best practices when adding or changing schemes.

## Conventions

- One main screen per file under `app/`; shared UI goes in `components/`.
- Use `+not-found.tsx` for 404; use `_layout.tsx` at each level to define tabs or stack for that segment.
